    <!-- The corporate courier stops a few paces away, one hand half-raised, eyes darting between you and the way he came. He tries to hold a professional posture, but the fingers resting on his holster keep trembling.\n\n\"Easy... everyone stay easy. The name's {COURIER} - just a courier, the kind with an employee number stitched into his sleeve.\" He licks his cracked lips. \"The ship broke up in orbit. The cargo scattered across the crash site. I've been walking three days on this leg, trying to find it before the system logs me as a runner...\"\n\nHe lets out a small, bitter laugh. \"Listen to me, pouring it all out. Here's the deal - the diary and the restraint keys I'm carrying are yours. Write the cargo off as 'lost in transit.' Let me walk, and nobody reports this upstairs. What do you say, {NEGOTIATOR}? Better for both of us.\" -->
    <Mugirl.CourierDialogText>“劳驾，打听一下。两位雪牛娘，你们见过吧？我是押这趟货的，叫{COURIER}。”\n\n他撑着膝盖喘了口气，见你没接话，又赶紧补了一句：“别紧张，我没说要带她们走。船都摔成那样了，我上哪儿再找一艘？公司倒好，先问货，再问钥匙，最后问我还能不能接着送。”\n\n他从兜里摸出一串束具钥匙，攥了攥，递到你面前。\n\n“都在这儿，一把不留。她们身上的束具，你们拿这个开。按规矩我得把钥匙交回去……算了，就当给你们添麻烦的赔礼。”\n\n他往前凑了凑，压低声音：“{NEGOTIATOR}，帮我个忙。回去我就报货没找着，公司要是问起来，你们也别提钥匙的事。真让我照价赔，我这辈子的工资都得搭进去。东西你们收好，让我走，行吗？”</Mugirl.CourierDialogText>
